quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  17,87,"But on account of mercy from your Lord (We have not taken it away from your community). Indeed, His grace upon you (O Prophet) has (always) been abundant."
  17,88,"Say: ‘If (all) humans and jinn were to come together to bring the equivalent of this Qur’an, they could not produce the like of it, even if they supported one another.’"
  17,89,"And surely, We have repeatedly employed for the people in this Qur’an all kinds of examples. Yet most people refuse everything except disbelief."
  17,90,And they say: ‘We shall never believe you (O Muhammad s) until you make a spring gush out for us from the ground.
  17,91,"Or until you have a garden of date palms and grapes, and you should cause streams to flow, gushing out through it."
  17,92,"Or until you cause the heaven to fall upon us in pieces, just as you have claimed, or until you bring Allah and the angels right in front of us."
  17,93,"Or until you have a house of gold, or you ascend into heaven. And we will not believe your ascension until you bring us down a Book we can read.’ Say: ‘Glory be to my Lord! Am I anything but a human being (and) a Messenger?’"
  17,94,"And nothing has prevented (these) people from believing when the guidance has come to them, except that they say: ‘Has Allah sent a human as a messenger?’"
  17,95,"Say: ‘If there were angels on the earth, walking around as residents, We would have certainly sent down to them from heaven an angel as a messenger.’"
  17,96,"Say: ‘Allah is sufficient as a Witness between me and you. Indeed, He is All-Aware, All-Seeing of His servants."
